&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll be joining Carta&#39;s People &amp;amp; Workplace Experience team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;Singapore is Carta&#39;s primary Asia hub and a cornerstone of the company&#39;s international growth. The Workplace Experience team ensures that every Carta employee — from a day-one new hire to a visiting executive — has the physical environment, operational infrastructure, and human support they need to do their best work. This team sits within the broader People organization and partners closely with IT, Recruiting, and Finance to keep offices running smoothly across geographies. As Carta&#39;s regional footprint expands, this team&#39;s work grows in both complexity and consequence — and this role sits at the center of it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;ul1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Operationally self-sufficient. You have 3+ years of experience in office management, workplace experience, or facilities coordination — ideally in a tech startup or fast-paced corporate environment — and you run things without waiting to be told.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;People-first professional. You bring warmth and polish to every interaction, whether welcoming a visitor, resolving an employee request, or navigating a vendor issue under pressure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Regionally adaptable. You&#39;re comfortable working across cultures and time zones, and you&#39;re ready and willing to travel within APAC on short notice when business needs arise.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Tech-fluent. You&#39;re confident in Google Workspace, Slack, Zoom, and modern guest and access control systems such as Envoy and keycard management platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Clear, confident communicator. You write and speak in English with precision and professionalism, and you manage upward, across teams, and with external partners with equal ease.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
