&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll be joining our Carta Law team, specifically within the Emerging Company Venture Capital (ECVC) function.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our ECVC team manages the end-to-end process for early-stage financing deals, representing both emerging companies and the venture capital funds that invest in them. Working alongside paralegals and other attorneys, you&#39;ll own day-to-day client relationships and serve as the primary point of contact for fundraising transactions. This role partners closely with top-tier law firms, accelerators, and venture firms to deliver consistent, high-quality legal support to founders and investors at the earliest stages of company building.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Problems You&#39;ll Solve&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Carta, our employees set out on a mission to unlock the power of equity ownership for more people in more places. We believe that the problems we solve today unlock the opportunities of tomorrow. As a Senior Lawyer - Venture Financings, you&#39;ll work to:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary point of contact for founders, venture capital funds, and their respective outside counsel, coordinating term sheet negotiation, diligence, signing, and post-closing deliverables&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review and negotiate financing documents — SAFEs, convertible notes, and NVCA-form Stock Purchase Agreements, Investors&#39; Rights Agreements, Voting Agreements, and ROFR/Co-Sale Agreements for priced rounds — advising on cap table, governance, and corporate matters that arise from each transaction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supervise and mentor paralegals through complex early-stage financing transactions — SAFEs, convertible notes, and a company&#39;s first priced equity round — ensuring documentation is accurate, timely, and aligned with client playbooks and market-standard terms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and evolve deal playbooks and negotiation parameters, alongside the MD, across company- and fund-side client engagements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and deepen trusted relationships with founders, venture funds, accelerators, and outside counsel, positioning Carta Law as the go-to partner for early-stage financing work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support business development by contributing to new client pitches alongside the Growth team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the technology team to continuously improve AI-driven legal delivery tools and workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for someone who is:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experienced in ECVC law.&lt;/strong&gt; You have a strong background in early-stage financings — SAFEs, convertible notes, and priced equity rounds — and can independently manage complex, fast-moving deal processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Client-focused and commercially minded.&lt;/strong&gt; You build strong relationships with founders, venture capital funds, and their counsel, and know how to communicate clearly under pressure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A natural leader and mentor.&lt;/strong&gt; You have experience supervising paralegals, and can manage team output across multiple simultaneous deals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Detail-driven and execution-focused.&lt;/strong&gt; You thrive on getting deals done – you prioritize effectively, handle competing deadlines, and do not lose momentum.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tech-savvy.&lt;/strong&gt; You are comfortable working with AI-backed legal tools and are curious about the role of technology in modern legal delivery. We&#39;re especially open to candidates who are extremely tech-savvy and have a genuine interest in how AI can productize the legal ecosystem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Licensed to practice.&lt;/strong&gt; You are qualified to practice in California or a comparable jurisdiction. 7+ years of relevant experience recommended.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
