&lt;p&gt;For more information about our offices and culture, check out our &lt;a href=&quot;https://carta.com/careers/&quot;&gt;Carta careers page&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Team You&#39;ll Work With&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll be joining our Carta Law team, specifically within the Contracts - APAC function. Carta Law is the largest AI-native law firm for private capital, born from the combination of Avantia Law and Carta. Our Contracts team manages the full lifecycle of commercial contracts for clients – from first review through to execution.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to a Supervising Lawyer in the region, you&#39;ll work alongside fellow paralegals and lawyers and embedded AI agents. This team delivers high volumes of pre-M&amp;amp;A contract work at speed, supported by AI-backed tools including Carta&#39;s proprietary platform, Ava.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Problems You&#39;ll Solve&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Carta, our employees set out on a mission to unlock the power of equity ownership for more people in more places. We believe that the problems we solve today unlock the opportunities of tomorrow. As a Paralegal in the Contracts team, you&#39;ll work to:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Keep contracts moving.&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Own the prompt intake and first-round markup of investment-related NDAs and related documents, ensuring nothing sits in a queue longer than it should and tight client turnaround times are consistently met&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Make the process more effective.&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Support Carta&#39;s UK lawyers with first-round drafting and ad hoc legal work — handling the volume so attorneys can focus on the complexity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build workflows clients can rely on.&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Set up and coordinate client workflows, manage document portals, and drive contracts through to execution, giving clients a seamless, professional experience at every step.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hold the quality bar.&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Deliver crisp, commercially sound contract support that reflects Carta&#39;s reputation for precision — balancing speed with the attention to detail that private capital clients expect&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experienced in transactional legal work.&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;You have 2+ years of experience recommended working within a transactional or corporate practice group, or an in-house commercial legal team — with hands-on exposure to commercial contracts and investment-related NDA drafting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fast and precise under pressure&lt;/strong&gt;.&amp;nbsp;You thrive in high-volume, deadline-driven environments — you can context-switch between competing demands without letting quality slip.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Commercially and legally grounded.&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;You have a strong grasp of relevant legal concepts and the commercial pragmatism to apply them — you know when to flag something and when to just get it done.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A clear communicator.&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Your written and verbal communication is crisp and concise — clients and colleagues get what they need from you without having to ask twice.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A self-starter with a builder&#39;s mindset.&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;You take ownership, spot inefficiencies, and look for ways to improve how the team operates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Familiar with private markets.&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Exposure to private capital, fund structures, or investor onboarding workflows is a strong plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Desirable requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tech-forward. &lt;/strong&gt;You&#39;re proficient with AI-backed contract review tools like Carta Ava, CLM/e-signature systems, and look for ways to improve them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Language capability.&lt;/strong&gt; Able to review and negotiate in Japanese, Korean or Mandarin&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
